<title>SWEDEN: NCC to open jointly run SE Asia offices.</title>
<headline>NCC to open jointly run SE Asia offices.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company NCC said on Monday it had signed an agreement with two other European builders, Germany's Strabag and Italy's Impregilo to cooperate in Southeast Asia.</p>
<p>This will involve opening joint representational offices in Manila in the Philippines and in Jakarta, Indonesia.</p>
<p>A number of NCC employees will be stationed in the new offices, NCC said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Together with Strabag and Impregilo, we will now have the know-how and resources to undertake large-scale projects in Southeast Asia,&quot; NCC's chief executive Jan Sjoqvist said in the statement.</p>
<p>NCC, Strabag and Impregilo are members of a construction consortium currently engaged in final negotiations regarding a major highway project in Poland worth nearly 25 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
</text>
